{
  "openapi": "3.1.1",
  "info": {
    "title": "OpenAsy Incidents API",
    "version": "0.5.0",
    "summary": "Run an incident: timeline, tasks, evidence and a postmortem.",
    "description": "Every screen of incidents uses this API, and so can your scripts and the other products (ADR 0014, 0023). Within `/api/v1` changes are additive only; anything removed is deprecated first (ADR 0024). Errors use Problem Details (RFC 9457).\n\nEverything takes the session of a signed-in person or an API token, and each operation names the role it needs (`x-openasy-role`: viewer, editor, admin; ADR 0003). Other products open incidents with an API token that has the editor role.\n\nSign-in, members and API tokens are under `/api/v1/auth`, provided by [@openasy/auth](https://github.com/openasy/auth#routes).",
    "license": {
      "name": "AGPL-3.0-only",
      "identifier": "AGPL-3.0-only"
    }
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "/",
      "description": "This incidents"
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Incidents",
      "description": "Open, change and close an incident."
    },
    {
      "name": "Timeline",
      "description": "What happened, in order. Append-only."
    },
    {
      "name": "Tasks",
      "description": "What has to be done, and by whom."
    },
    {
      "name": "Evidence",
      "description": "Links to where the evidence lives."
    },
    {
      "name": "Postmortem",
      "description": "What was learned, written after the incident."
    },
    {
      "name": "Product",
      "description": "Version and overview of this incidents."
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/api/v1/incidents": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "listIncidents",
        "tags": [
          "Incidents"
        ],
        "summary": "List incidents",
        "security": [
          {
            "session": []
          },
          {
            "apiToken": []
          },
          {
            "adminToken": []
          }
        ],
        "description": "Needs the viewer role.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "status",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "description": "`active` is everything not resolved.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "active",
                "open",
                "investigating",
                "mitigated",
                "resolved"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "severity",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Comma-separated severities, such as `critical,high`.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "product",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Only incidents that involve this product.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "q",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Matches the title, summary, commander or key.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "maxLength": 128
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "limit",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Page size.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1,
              "maximum": 500,
              "default": 100
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "cursor",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "description": "The previous page's nextCursor.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Active incidents first, the most serious first.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/IncidentList"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          },
          "422": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          },
          "503": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          }
        },
        "x-openasy-role": "viewer"
      },
      "post": {
        "operationId": "createIncident",
        "tags": [
          "Incidents"
        ],
        "summary": "Open an incident",
        "security": [
          {
            "session": []
          },
          {
            "apiToken": []
          },
          {
            "adminToken": []
          }
        ],
        "description": "People open incidents here, and so do other products with an API token (ADR 0023). A product sets `external` so one problem is one incident however often it reports.\n\n```bash\ncurl -sf -X POST -H \"Authorization: Bearer $INCIDENTS_API_TOKEN\" -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"title\":\"Brute force on vpn\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"products\":[\"siem\",\"vpn\"],\"external\":{\"source\":\"siem\",\"reference\":\"sig-42\"}}' \\\n  https://incidents.example.com/api/v1/incidents\n```\n\nNeeds the editor role.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/NewIncident"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "An incident with this external source and reference exists; a note was added to its timeline.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Incident"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "201": {
            "description": "Opened.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Incident"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          },
          "422": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          },
          "503": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          }
        },
        "x-openasy-role": "editor"
      }
    },
